| Buoys block a completing jump (Phase 18, D-09) | Supersedes "Keep the buoys non-blocking in Phase 12". Oolite's `checkShipsInVicinityForWitchJumpExit` tests every ship but the player, whatever its scan class, by `0.1 x [ship mass] > d^2` and `d^2 < SCANNER_MAX_RANGE2` (`ShipEntity.m:12498-12531`), so the witchpoint beacon and the nav buoy block; quick task 261117-lka measured the nav buoy blocking at 263.3 m and clear at 265.3 m. Wegolite: both buoys use `NAV_BUOY_MASS` = 698,691.1875 (the composite compiled into `ships-client.json` entry `buoy`, pinned by a test; blockage radius 264.33 m). PD-02: the check uses the buoy's live position, its layout position plus `World.buoys.<key>.offset`. PD-01: its live mass; once its subentity is detached Oolite's GLfloat `mass -= [sub mass]` (`ShipEntity.m:8194`) leaves the float32 691,044.375 (`NAV_BUOY_HULL_MASS`, equal to the compiled hull-only mass), radius 262.88 m. D-05: a destroyed buoy never blocks. Liveness, offset and attachment come from the previous tick's world through `ShipField.buoy(key)`, as every field query does; without a world both buoys count as alive, unmoved and whole. Order: the station, the witchpoint buoy, the nav buoy, then NPC ships; each refusal clears the target and spends no fuel or jump time. The mass reaches the step as `StepOptions.hyperspace.buoyMass`, exactly as `stationMass`: `buildStepOptions` always supplies it, and world-less unit flights and the frozen worlds omit it, so their pins hold; a missing, non-finite or non-positive mass blocks nothing. The HUD names the blocker as Oolite's `witch-blocked` string does: "Witchspace jump aborted: too close to Navigation Buoy" (53 characters) and "Witchspace jump aborted: too close to Witchpoint Beacon" (55). The beacon wording is final by owner decision 2026-11-20, which raised the HUD message budget `MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS` from 54 to 55 (55 glyphs at 23.2 px and 0.6 em are 765.6 design px, centred on x = 1248 of 1920; raised again to 60 the same day by owner decision, so the two docking bounce lines and the default pitch/roll hint fit whole); the 18-07 executor's interim "too near Witchpoint Beacon" (51) is gone. Oolite's own "Witchspace jump aborted (too close to [blockerName])." (`descriptions.plist:503`) waits for the HUD word wrap (`printLongText:`, `GuiDisplayGen.m:736-794`): todo 2026-11-20-hud-message-word-wrap-like-oolite, with the tripwire `tests/guards/hud-message-length.test.ts`. Arrival: Oolite places every arrival at least `safeWitchspaceExitDistance`, the witchpoint buoy's collision radius plus 750 m = 809.14 m, from it (`PlayerEntity.m:6913-6928`, `Universe.m:2843-2851`), so an immediate re-jump after arrival is not refused by the witchpoint buoy, and Wegolite matches; every arrival, launch and Load creates a new world whose buoys are pristine, so a buoy moved in one world cannot reach the next arrival. `tests/sim/world/buoy-clearance.test.ts` sweeps all 2,048 layouts: the whole arrival shell and the launch pose stay farther than the blockage radius plus both hull radii (396.16 m) from both buoys. D-08: pods and plates never block (they have no entry in the NPC mass list) and never mass-lock, and buoys never mass-lock (`CLASS_CARGO`, `CLASS_BUOY`, `PlayerEntity.m:3044-3061`); Oolite's loop is class-free, so a pod within 9.97 m and a plate within 5.23 m of the player's centre would block there (plan 18-20 measured the rule on a cargo-class surrogate), a divergence that can matter only while the piece sits inside the Cobra's hull. Follow-up: the torus factor's nearest surface (`src/sim/flight/torus.ts:53-71`) still reads the layout buoys, so a destroyed witchpoint beacon still caps the factor and a moved buoy counts at its layout position, while Oolite takes the nearest live collidable entity (`PlayerEntity.m:2917-2924`); recorded in FIDELITY.md and the todo 2026-11-20-torus-nearest-surface-live-buoys. Reversible: an option and two blocker kinds | ✓ Phase 18 plan 18-07 (D-05, D-08, D-09, PD-01, PD-02; beacon copy final, owner decision 2026-11-20) |
| The hyperspace-failure fixture pose leaves the witchpoint buoy (Phase 18, D-06, owner sanction) | With blocking buoys, `tests/e2e/hyperspace-failure.spec.ts` would complete its countdown 0 m from the witchpoint buoy and be refused. The owner sanctioned one edit (D-06): `ORIGIN_POSE.position` moves from `[0, 0, 0]` to `[1000, 0, 0]`, with its comment, and nothing else in the spec changes; the spec's own pre-H assertion (more than 7,000 m from the station) stays. At Lave the new pose is 1,000 m from the witchpoint buoy (outside its 59.14 m hull and the 264.3 m blockage radius plus both hull radii, 396.1 m), 434,885 m from the station (blockage radius 7,179.7 m) and 436,269 m from the nav buoy. The spec is traffic-off, so no hull table loads and no collision can move the buoy. The pose is justified for Lave only, where the spec parks the player; the generality check is the 2,048-layout clearance sweep of `tests/sim/world/buoy-clearance.test.ts`. It is the only browser-spec edit of Phase 18 | ✓ Phase 18 plan 18-07 (owner sanction D-06) |
