| Collisions follow Oolite's collideWithShip, octree against octree (Phase 18, CBT-18) | The collision stage (`resolveCollisions`, `src/sim/combat/collide.ts`) runs inside `resolveShots` after the laser hits are queued and before the one ledger, and only with `CombatOptions.collisions`: the app sets it in `buildStepOptions`, the frozen acceptance harness never does, so its worlds stay byte-identical (PITFALLS 4, QUAL-11). Colliders: the in-flight player with its hull (excluded while launching, A3, a divergence: Oolite's player `canCollide` is YES while launching, `PlayerEntity.m:2242-2254`), live NPC ships with a hull and a compiled mass, and live pods and plates with their `debrisMassOf` mass; never a wreck (`canCollide`). Broad phase: a sweep on x with Oolite's strict sphere test `d^2 < (r1 + r2)^2` (`CollisionRegion.m`), then `doOctreesCollide` with Oolite's prime, the body first in the z list (the row "The octree test's prime follows Oolite's z order" below; plan 18-11 had made the lower-ranked body the prime, corrected by owner decision 2026-11-20). Order: `colliderRank` puts the player first and every other body by ascending squared distance from the player, ties by id, a non-finite distance last, after Oolite's update order over `sortedEntities` (`Universe.m:6439, 6534`, kept sorted by `zero_distance` at `6557-6567`, an exact sort here); each body then runs its own collision list in rank order, as `manageCollisions` does (`ShipEntity.m:10991-11017`): a call that collides removes self from the other's list (`11149-11150`), a call that returns early because the pair separates faster than 1 m/s leaves it, and the other calls in its own turn. Response: `collideWithShip` (plan 18-16, `ShipEntity.m:11020-11152`): velocity and position changes apply at once in call order while the damage joins the one ledger as `"scrape"` records after the laser records (A5), each with a copy of the source's position at queue time (the Phase 15 `sourcePosition` rule); the player's share goes through `routeScrapeDamage` (the shield on the other's side, then energy, no cabin heat). A ship at 0 dies through `killShip` with its debris, a pod or plate is removed, and a same-tick mutual ram kill keeps the existing ledger credit rule (the D-10 asymmetry). The destroyed flags read each body's energy before this tick's ledger. The station is not a collider: touching its hull stays the dock's damage-free contact (DOCK-09) and NPCs and pods pass through it. The player is never `destroyable` before Phase 20 (`PLAYER_NOT_DESTROYABLE_UNTIL_PHASE_20`). No `shipCollided` script event or `COLLISION` AI message (RESEARCH A8). No random draw: `takeScrapeDamage`'s fragment roll only sets `being_mined`, which only asteroids read (`ShipEntity.m:11659-11667`). PD-05: `canScoop` (`ShipEntity.m:11022-11027, 11183-11197`) is out of phase, so a rammed pod takes damage and dies above 15.3 m/s against the player. Since plan 18-18 the two buoys are colliders as Oolite's movers (PD-02): each live buoy whose `buoy` hull is loaded joins with its static id (4, 5), its pose `buoyPosition` and `buoyOrientation(flightTime)`, its drift as total velocity, its `World.staticHealth` as energy and `destroyable`; its share of a response goes to `World.buoys.<key>.velocity` (held to `MAX_ENTITY_VELOCITY`) and `.offset` (held to `MAX_BUOY_OFFSET`), and it then brakes by its own thrust (plan 18-17), so a 100 m/s ram carries the nav buoy the 8.333 m nudge plus 9.583 m of braking. A ram above about 241.3 m/s by the player (`dam2 = 214,737.6875 v^2 / 5e7 > 250`) destroys the buoy through `destroyBuoy`, credited to the player; a destroyed buoy is no collider and never moves. The frangible subentity answers a contact the hull does not make (PD-01): the other party is then the subentity (mass `BUOY_SUBENTITY_MASS` 7,646.7861328125, energy `subentityEnergy`, the buoy's velocity as the parent's, `ShipEntity.m:11057-11067`), dam2 goes whole to the subentity's id (6, 7) as a scrape record with no 1 % bleed-through on the buoy (`ShipEntity.m:11123-11128`; `takeScrapeDamage` has none, `11639-11673`; the bleed is the laser rule), and the buoy takes `dvOtherBody`, also when the rammer dies. Divergence: the C's nudge of a contacted subentity moves the subentity inside its parent (`ShipEntity.m:11143-11146`); Wegolite keeps it at its authored offset. A detached subentity takes no part, and the buoy's collision mass becomes `NAV_BUOY_HULL_MASS` (691,044.375, the float32 the C holds after `subEntityDied` subtracts the subentity's mass, `ShipEntity.m:8194`). When the buoy is self the contact is the buoy body's. Measured: only a pod or plate inside the buoy hull's cavity can touch the subentity alone; a ship's hull always meets the buoy's hull first. Buoys follow `colliderRank` like every collider; buoy-buoy pairs use the same rule and are unreachable in practice (the buoys are at least 223,595 m apart in every layout). The 18-20 anti-conjoin push is not reproduced for the buoy either (the FIDELITY row "Each body runs its own collision list"). The nav buoy 10 km ahead of the dock on the launch axis is met by a straight departure: the launch leaves the slot at 175 m/s, so with idle controls the player rams it about 54 s after launch (dam1 about 428 on the player, dam2 about 131.5 on the buoy), and at 350 m/s the ram deals the player about 1,712 damage and destroys the buoy, so `otherDestroyed` reverses the player's 631 m/s rebound and no net rebound remains, as plan 18-20 measured on real Oolite (where the player is destroyed too). Since plan 18-21 a steered NPC sees each live buoy in the proximity pass and turns away once alerted (PD-06, PD-08, the row below); contact remains possible, as in Oolite. Tripwire (owner rule 2026-11-18): the player's deferred inelastic reversal is the todo `2026-11-19-collision-reversal-on-player-death`, and `tests/guards/collision-player-death.test.ts` fails, naming it, while `PLAYER_NOT_DESTROYABLE_UNTIL_PHASE_20` survives and a `playerDestroyed` producer, a new `FlightMode` member or a changed ledger floor appears. Cost: `CollisionStats` pins the sweep and narrow-phase counts at the entity cap (`tests/sim/combat/collision-cost.test.ts`). Reversible: the opt-in flag | ✓ Phase 18 plan 18-11. ✓ Plan 18-18: a 100 m/s ram matches `collide-player-buoy-100` and carries the buoy 17.917 m; 250 m/s destroys it; the cavity contact damages id 7; 30/60/144 Hz hash equal (`tests/sim/combat/collision-buoy.test.ts`, `tests/sim/world/collision-cadence.test.ts`) |
