| Drift beside the engine speed (Phase 18, D-02) | The player carries Oolite's Newtonian `velocity` as `FlightState.drift` beside the scalar engine speed, and NPC ships and buoys carry theirs as `velocity` (plans 18-10 and 18-17). The player's drift moves the position every in-flight tick and is power-braked in float32 by the raw thrust 32 times the thrust factor with the cleanup terms (`PlayerEntity.m:3387-3405`); an NPC's by `5 x thrust x dt` only for non-zero thrust (`ShipEntity.m:5817-5824`), in one pass after the steering loop (an ordering difference from Oolite's per-entity update). A zero drift is never hashed (criterion 5) and every pose install zeroes it. The collision stage writes it (D-01). At the station, a drifting player meets the dock face through plan 18-10's own contact rule, which reflects the drift's inward part with restitution 0.5 (`BOUNCE_RESTITUTION`), where Oolite runs `collideWithShip` with the station's mass and its `adjustVelocity:` override that never moves the station (`ShipEntity.m:11089`, `StationEntity.m:1159-1163`): a divergence, kept because the station is not a collider (DOCK-09). Reversible: the drift fields are pristine-omitted | ✓ Phase 18 plans 18-10, 18-11, 18-17 |
| The explosion blast pushes ships, buoys and the player (Phase 18, D-03, PD-02) | Supersedes "The explosion's blast pushes debris only". Oolite's `becomeExplosion` deals momentum for every exploding ship (`dealMomentumWithinDesiredRange:0.125f * mass` with `desired_range = collision_radius * 2.5f`, `ShipEntity.m:8121-8126`), and after a lethal ram `collideWithShip` reverses the survivor's own rebound (D-03), so the blast is what throws the survivor clear. Rule (`src/sim/world/debris.ts`, `blastImpulse` and `blastFrom`): every receiver whose centre is strictly within `desired_range + r` of the source (`Universe.m:5862-5868`, the C's float compare) gets `dv = amount x desired_range / d2 / m` along the unit vector from the source, with `d2 = |p|^2 - r^2` floored at 0.1 (`ShipEntity.m:7686-7690`) and `r`, `m` the RECEIVER's collision radius and mass (`addImpactMoment`, `11178-11181`); a receiver at the source's centre gets no push (a zero direction); every component is clamped at `MAX_ENTITY_VELOCITY` at the write and a zero push writes nothing, so a kill with nothing movable in range hashes as before. The magnitude stays in double, within about 1e-7 of the C's float arithmetic. Receivers, in ascending id: the two live buoys (ids 4, 5; `NAV_BUOY_MASS` while the subentity is attached, `NAV_BUOY_HULL_MASS` once detached, the layout radius, `World.buoys.<key>.velocity`), the player (id 100) only in flight, its push accumulated (`BlastPush`) and added to `FlightState.drift` once after the tick's kills, live NPC ships by their hull-table mass (a ship without one is not pushed), and every pod, plate and wreck by `debrisMassOf`. Never the victim (dead before its blast), a destroyed buoy or the station. Sources: a destroyed ship (as in Phase 16), a destroyed pod or plate (its model mass and radius, `killShip`'s cargo branch), a destroyed buoy as two sources in the C's order (its subentity while attached, from the buoy's centre with `BUOY_SUBENTITY_MASS` and `BUOY_SUBENTITY_RADIUS` 25.822647094726562, then the hull with `NAV_BUOY_HULL_MASS` 691,044.375 and the layout radius 59.13554763793945, `ShipEntity.m:8115-8126, 8185-8194`), and a buoy subentity on the tick a pulse or a ram brings it to 0 (`ShipEntity.m:7895-7904`; its parent gets no push, a zero direction). All only with debris content (traffic on); the frozen acceptance harness has none. The 18-03 fixtures (`tests/oracles/combat/response/fixtures/blast.json`), quoted: a Krait killed with the player's centre 10 m away takes the floor, `dv` (40.889225006103516, 0, 54.51896286010742), 68.15 m/s; a Krait and a Shuttle just touching, 0.026917003095149994 m/s on the Shuttle; a Krait and the player just touching, 0.0006941189058125019 m/s; a pod beside a pod 8 m away, 0.059654805809259415 m/s; a pod 5 m away, inside the receiver's radius, takes the floor, (10.872424125671387, 14.496565818786621, 0); a dying buoy: a pod at 100 m gets the hull's (0.7739403247833252, 1.0319204330444336, 0) only, the player 100 m away -0.00006094400305300951 from the subentity plus -0.012612634338438511 from the hull, -0.01267357834149152 m/s; a Shuttle at 148.23982232138232 m is out and one at 148.2398223213823 m (one ulp nearer) is in. Divergences (FIDELITY): the station is no receiver (in Oolite it is one, braked to rest within the frame; the same result); Oolite also pushes a launching player (`isInSpace` lists `STATUS_LAUNCHING`, `Entity.m:1038`); a wreck that burns out explodes in Oolite and does not here. Reversible: the receiver and source lists in `blastFrom`, `killShip`, `destroyBuoy` and `resolveShots` | ✓ Phase 18 plan 18-19: every 18-03 blast fixture passes through `blastImpulse` and the world pass (`tests/sim/world/blast.oracle.test.ts`); the hand cases in `tests/sim/world/kill.test.ts`, `tests/sim/world/debris.test.ts` and `tests/sim/combat/step.test.ts`; a kill pushing the player, a Shuttle and the nav buoy hashes equal at 30, 60 and 144 Hz (`tests/sim/world/debris-cadence.test.ts`); no pin moved |
